    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d173">

                <pb facs="0381" n="361" xml:id="pg361"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1165.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1864-11-30"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 30, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I enclose herewith a copy of the
                    correspondence which has taken place between Mr. Allen, United States consul at
                    Bermuda, and the authorities of those islands, relative to the capture of the
                    steamer Roanoke by the insurgents. You are instructed to make known to her
                    Britannic Majesty’s government the facts therein mentioned, and to protest
                    against the proceedings at Bermuda in enlisting the men and discharging the
                    accused parties; the protest to apply particularly to Braine, who was concerned
                    in the affair of the Chesapeake, and whose delivery was refused.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d173-a1.xml" xpointer="d173-a1"/>
            </div>
